-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/1f1a4c9c-70c0-4a95-ba6f-9aa23250ea93
-- title:
--   Corollary 4.12 — an $M$-bad prefix with probability at least $\varepsilon/2$ ($k\ge1$)
-- statement:
--   Let $n=k+m$ with $k\ge1$, let $|\psi\rangle$ be a pure state with $\mathcal F_{\mathsf{Stab}}(\psi)\le1-\varepsilon$, and let $M$ be a Lagrangian subspace. In a round that applies a uniformly random Clifford $C$ and then partial Bell difference sampling, the probability of an $M$-bad prefix (one with no completion in $C(M)$) is at least $\varepsilon/2$:
--
--   $$1-\mathbb E_C\big[Q^k_{C\psi}(H_{C(M)})\big]\ge\frac{\varepsilon}{2}.$$
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: n qubits with m = n − k → k + m qubits; reason: the same instances; the paper's m := n − k
--   - generalization: M: any Lagrangian subspace that contains M_0 (p. 32) → every Lagrangian subspace M; reason: the proof (via Proposition 4.11) uses only that M is Lagrangian; specializes to the paper's M
--   - generalization: ε > 0 (standing assumption of Theorem 4.1) → any real ε; reason: for ε ≤ 0 the claim is that a probability is at least ε/2 ≤ 0; specializes to ε > 0
--   - encoding: the probability that partial Bell sampling outputs an M-bad prefix in a random-Clifford round → 1 − E_C[Q^k_{Cψ}(H_{C(M)})]; reason: the identification made in the proof of Corollary 4.12
--   - encoding: a random Clifford → the uniform average over the finite group generated by Had, S and CNOT; reason: this is the paper's Clifford group (p. 14)
--   - encoding: stabilizer state: a maximal Abelian subgroup of Paulis with P|ψ⟩ = ±|ψ⟩ → a unit vector fixed by a commuting subgroup of the Pauli group of order 2^n not containing −I; reason: the signs χ(u) are absorbed into the group elements ±P_u; same states
--   - encoding: F_Stab = max over Stab → sSup of the set of overlaps; reason: the set is nonempty, bounded and finite-valued, so the supremum is the maximum
-- source:
--   Arunachalam, Schatzki, Optimal stabilizer testing and learning with limited quantum memory, arXiv:2607.02444 (version of 2 Nov 2026), Corollary 4.12, p. 35

import Definitions.Def_StabTestMem_prefixMass
import Definitions.Def_StabTestMem_cliffordAvg
import Definitions.Def_StabTestMem_cliffordImage
import Definitions.Def_StabTestMem_IsLagrangian
import Definitions.Def_StabTestMem_stabFidelity

namespace StabTestMem

open QAlgorithms

/-- **Corollary 4.12: a bad prefix with probability at least `ε/2` (`k ≥ 1`).** Arunachalam, Schatzki, *Optimal stabilizer testing and learning with limited quantum memory*, arXiv:2607.02444 (version of 2 Nov 2026), Corollary
4.12, p. 35: "Assume F_stab(ψ) ≤ 1 − ε and k ≥ 1. Then, in a random-Clifford round, the probability
that partial Bell sampling outputs an M-bad prefix is at least ε/2."

The probability of an `M`-bad prefix in a random-Clifford round is `1 − E_C[Q_{Cψ}(H_{C(M)})]` (proof
of Corollary 4.12: "The M-good prefixes are exactly the prefix projection H_M").

**Formalization Note.** `n = k + m`; `M` is any Lagrangian subspace (the paper applies it to "any
Lagrangian subspace M that contains M_0", p. 32; the proof uses only that `M` is Lagrangian).
`ε` is any real number (for `ε ≤ 0` the claim is that a probability is at least `ε/2 ≤ 0`). -/
theorem badPrefix_prob_ge_half {k m : ℕ} (hk : 1 ≤ k)
    (ψ : EuclideanSpace ℂ (Qubits (k + m))) (hψ : IsState ψ) (ε : ℝ)
    (hF : stabFidelity ψ ≤ 1 - ε)
    (M : Submodule (ZMod 2) (CutRankSched.Pauli (k + m))) (hM : IsLagrangian M) :
    ε / 2 ≤ 1 - cliffordAvg (fun C =>
      prefixMass (act (C : Matrix (Qubits (k + m)) (Qubits (k + m)) ℂ) ψ)
        (cliffordImage C (M : Set (CutRankSched.Pauli (k + m))))) := by sorry

end StabTestMem
